    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the S$4.50 no-show cancellation fee stands, and the driver is paid S$3.60 (80% of the fee in force). On a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling, amount_sgd carries the same figure as driver_compensation_sgd per POL-GEN-03; the rider's charge is left in place and the S$3.60 is what this ruling moves.\n\nWhy the fee is chargeable (POL-NS-01). All four conditions hold on the instruments. (a) EV-TRIP-02702 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 16:55:03. (b) EV-GPS-02702 places the driver inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup (Tampines Mall) in 42 consecutive qualifying fixes, his nearest fix being 0.16 m from the pin. (c) His in-geofence dwell is one continuous run of 409 seconds, from 16:55:03 to 17:01:52, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as the clause requires; that exceeds the 180-second free waiting period in force (EV-TRIP-02702 platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no longer no_show_threshold_sec is set, and the older zone minimum_dwell_sec is not applied to a record that carries platform_policy). (d) The record shows no boarding and termination by the driver at 17:01:56 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, 233 seconds after the 180-second dwell elapsed at 16:58:03.\n\nThe arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: at the 16:55:03 marker timestamp the driver's nearest fix was 0.16 m from the pin and he was stationary, so the waiting clock is the marker clock and no false-arrival referral arises. POL-NS-06 does not bite: with a 409-second dwell against a 180-second minimum there is no shortfall, so no refund follows from that clause.\n\nThe rider's arguments. (1) You say you messaged 'coming down now' at 16:57:23 and the driver never replied, so POL-NS-04 should exonerate you. POL-NS-04 requires all three limbs, and limb (c) fails on your own device track in EV-GPS-02702: 69 fixes, all around 854 m from the pickup pin (min 853.88 m, max 861.38 m), none inside the 150 m rider-presence radius for a LARGE_VENUE zone. Because limb (c) is affirmatively failed, POL-NS-04 does not apply and the fee is decided under POL-NS-01. Your related point under POL-NS-11 is accepted: the rider track decides only whether POL-NS-04 exonerates you, it does not impair the driver's trace for arrival or dwell, and the driver's arrival and dwell stand on his own clean, complete track. (2) POL-NS-12 does not apply because the arrival marker is a driver-pressed BUTTON, so arrival is established from the exported trace under POL-NS-02; I decline your request to impose an extra accuracy requirement, because nothing in the record shows the 42 qualifying fixes lack a reported accuracy. (3) The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02702-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) makes any accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, but that clause needs a shortfall and there is none, so the point does not change the outcome. (4) POL-NS-03(ii) is not reached: the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong entrance outside it, so registered_pickup_points = 1 and the pin-ambiguity goodwill route does not arise.\n\nDriver compensation (POL-NS-07). POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so the driver is paid 80% of the S$4.50 fee in force = S$3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the 4-or-more limb. The fare ledger EV-FARE-02702 charges exactly S$4.50 with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, reconciling under POL-NS-08(d), so no integrity defect arises. No artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired, so the confidence cap is 1.00 and confidence is set at 0.90; the S$3.60 monetary effect is below the S$8.00 execution threshold and executes automatically. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
  },
